# PREVIEW — non-secret RUNTIME config (read from process.env by the server).
# Was fly.preview.toml [env]. See config/env/README.md and D-85. Genuine
# secrets stay in Infisical (infra/infisical/README.md, D-66).
#
# NODE_ENV / PORT are NOT here — they stay Fly/Docker-native (fly.<env>.toml
# [env] and the Dockerfile), because the platform, not the app, owns them.
#
# Nor is the split two-way. A THIRD bucket — every `*_R2_*`, `CHAT_AUDIO_R2_*`
# and `LIVEKIT_EGRESS_S3_*` var — is Tofu-owned and pushed directly to Fly
# (D-65), so it lives in neither this file nor Infisical and cannot be found by
# grepping the repo at all. That invisibility has already caused a wrong call:
# a reader concluded preview had no Egress config and predicted the recording
# E2E would fail, when all five vars were deployed. If a var the code reads is
# in neither this file nor infra/infisical/README.md's list, check
# `fly secrets list --app agendaprofe-preview` before concluding it is unset.

# Server-side Sentry/PostHog — identical values to their NEXT_PUBLIC_ twins in
# preview.build.env (Sentry DSNs and PostHog client keys are meant to be the
# same across server/client SDKs). POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY (a privileged
# phx_* key, different from this) stays in Infisical.
SENTRY_DSN=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_KEY=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# URLs / OAuth client ID / sender email — none of them credentials.
APP_URL=https://preview.spiralclass.com
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://preview.spiralclass.com
# D-138: left on the old domain, and note this is NOT symmetric with production.
# updates.staging.agendaprofe.com has never been a verified Resend domain — the
# account holds updates.agendaprofe.com and (since 2026-08-29)
# updates.spiralclass.com, and nothing else. So preview's sender was already
# unverified before the rename and this line changes nothing either way.
# Renaming it would only make the new domain look responsible for a gap that
# predates it. Fix by adding updates.staging.spiralclass.com in Resend, then
# moving this line — its DNS records are already in the new zone, though the
# DKIM one there is still the copied old-domain key and needs replacing.
RESEND_FROM=soporte@updates.staging.agendaprofe.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=__LOCAL__

# lib/csp.ts: nonce wiring verified complete; enforce mode on.
CSP_ENFORCE=1

# Legal-gated AI flags. D-94 enabled four of these on BOTH environments; D-114
# (2026-08-08) turned transcription and class recording back off on both; D-131
# (2026-08-26) turns those two back on — see the fuller note in
# production.runtime.env and D-131.
# Preview matches production deliberately: a capability that is off in
# production must not be exercisable on preview, or preview stops being a
# rehearsal of the real thing. Each flag still requires vendor keys (Infisical)
# to actually activate.
#
# ⚠️ Preview cannot currently rehearse the recording pipeline end-to-end even
# with this flag on: the shared LiveKit box posts webhooks to exactly one URL,
# production's (the box's own /home/ubuntu/oracle-livekit-production/livekit.yaml;
# was infra/oracle-runner/services/livekit.yaml.tftpl's, deleted D-139
# `webhook.urls`), so on preview an egress never gets finalised, no
# `lesson.audio.ready` fires, and nothing is transcribed. Recording itself
# starts and the file still lands in the preview R2 bucket. See D-131.
LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED=1
LIVE_CAPTIONS_ENABLED=1

# D-73 Layer 2/3: NOT under the D-21/D-22 legal gate (teacher's OWN public
# intro video, no student data/minors); needs DEEPGRAM_API_KEY (Infisical) +
# the teacher-videos R2 bucket to actually run.
INTRO_VIDEO_COACH_ENABLED=1

# AI-generated social-preview images (D-123) — also NOT under the D-21/D-22
# legal gate: a teacher's own marketing image for a share link, no student
# data involved. The upload half of social previews works with this flag off
# (D-123's default is upload-only); this flag turns on the Gemini-generated
# rail specifically. Still a no-op until GEMINI_VERTEX_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64
# (Infisical) is also set — socialPreviewAiEnabled() requires both (env.ts).
SOCIAL_PREVIEW_AI_ENABLED=1

# Vertex AI project the Gemini image-generation call runs against (D-127) —
# NOT a secret, same posture as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. Shared with production:
# it's a GCP project id, not an environment-scoped credential.
GEMINI_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=__LOCAL__

# LiveKit (in-class video call). The websocket URL is already handed to the
# client in the join grant, and API_KEY is only the identifier half of the
# pair — non-secret. LIVEKIT_API_SECRET (signs tokens) stays in Infisical;
# video calls and captions stay dark until that's also set.
#
# 2026-07-21: pointed at the self-hosted deployment
# (docs/deployment/ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md) instead of LiveKit Cloud — same
# RTC_PROVIDER="livekit" (LiveKitProvider talks to any LiveKit-API-compatible
# server, self-hosted or Cloud, per docs/features/live-calls-video.md).
# Zero app code changed for this swap, only these two values
# + the matching LIVEKIT_API_SECRET in Infisical. NOT yet reachable — the two
# manual infra steps (OCI security list, DNS for livekit.spiralclass.com) in
# ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md are still outstanding, so video will not
# actually connect until those are done. Rollback: revert this file back to
# the LiveKit Cloud values below (kept as a comment) + the matching Infisical
# secret, redeploy.
#   (LiveKit Cloud, pre-2026-07-21: LIVEKIT_URL=wss://<project>.livekit.cloud, LIVEKIT_API_KEY=<redacted>)
#
# Call RECORDING needs a THIRD set that is in neither place: recordingEnabled()
# also requires LIVEKIT_EGRESS_S3_{ACCESS_KEY,SECRET,BUCKET,ENDPOINT,REGION},
# which are Tofu-owned and pushed straight to Fly (D-65 — same as every other
# `*_R2_*` var; see infra/infisical/README.md's "Vars Infisical owns", which
# excludes them deliberately). They appear in NO file in this repo, so reading
# this one alone leads to the wrong conclusion that recording is unconfigured —
# it is configured on preview today, and self-hosted Egress uses these same
# per-request credentials unchanged (the box's Egress config carries no static
# storage config of its own — see infra/oracle-box/stack/). Confirm with `fly secrets list
# --app agendaprofe-preview` rather than grepping the repo.
# D-138: moved 2026-08-29 once the Oracle box actually held a certificate for
# livekit.spiralclass.com (Let's Encrypt via tls-alpn-01, expires 2026-11-27).
# Caddy still serves BOTH hostnames, so the old one keeps working for anything
# that has not picked this up.
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://livekit.spiralclass.com
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=__LOCAL__
# Selects the active VideoProvider (docs/features/live-calls-video.md).
# Explicit rather than left to the code-level default so a
# future flip to a second provider is a one-line diff here, not a guess about
# what "unset" currently means. lib/video/providers/index.ts
RTC_PROVIDER=livekit

# OFF as of D-114 (2026-08-08). It was turned on 2026-07-21 as part of the
# self-hosted migration — the ask then was working, validated recording, not
# infrastructure with the feature still dark, and real room-composite recording
# was tested against the self-hosted deployment
# (docs/deployment/ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md's "Confirmed findings"). That evidence
# still stands; it was not turned off for any defect. D-131 (2026-08-26) turns
# it back on.
# On = the teacher's Record control is shown on web and mobile and the server
# will start a room-composite egress to the preview `recordings` R2 bucket.
#
# The coupling this comment used to warn about (a pre-existing bug —
# turning recording on also started
# per-participant lesson-audio capture to R2 for consenting students) is fixed
# in D-114: maybeStartLessonAudioCapture requires transcriptionEnabled(), so
# that flag, not this one, is what decides whether any voice is captured.
CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED=1

# ── Commented out below: unset state IS the current live behavior (the
# code-level default). Uncommenting one is a real behavior change on next
# deploy — treat it like any other code change, not a secrets sync. Fill in
# only if/when you enable the corresponding feature; the paired real secrets
# still live in Infisical.
# STRIPE_TAX_ENABLED=1                   # has prerequisites outside the codebase
# LESSON_INSIGHTS_PRONUNCIATION_ENABLED=1  # needs AZURE_SPEECH_KEY/REGION (Infisical)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5        # optional override of the class-content/library compose model; this IS the default (D-87). NOTE: does NOT reach the hardcoded lesson-notes/intro-coach constants (those are claude-haiku-4-5, code-only). Any override MUST support output_config.effort — the compose call sites pass effort:"medium", which 400s on pre-4.6 models incl. claude-haiku-4-5
# CAPTION_TRANSLATION_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5  # optional override of the live-captions translation model; this IS the default
# GBP test-mode prices on the platform Stripe account's test product
# (prod_ExamplePreview0) — created via `stripe prices create` 2026-07-27,
# matching the GBP amounts in packages/shared's PLAN_PRICE_MINOR_UNITS_BY_CURRENCY
# (D-99). The old MXN test prices on this product were deactivated the same
# day. Uncommenting these turns ON subscription checkout on preview for the
# first time — it was dark before (no value was ever set here).
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_FOUNDING=__LOCAL__
# Preview's own (test-mode) Customer Portal configuration, applied by the same
# `pnpm --filter spiralclass-web stripe:portal:sync --apply` against preview.
# Pinned for the same reason production's is: so the portal a teacher meets
# here is the one this repo declares, and preview keeps testing what production
# will actually do.
STRIPE_BILLING_PORTAL_CONFIG_ID=__LOCAL__
# WISE_API_BASE=                         # defaults to production Wise API if unset
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=                # Calendar busy-import — distinct from GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (Sign-In) above
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
# FIELD_ENCRYPTION_REQUIRED=1            # DANGER: hard cutover, docs/security.md — do NOT set without a valid FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY live in Infisical; boot hard-fails otherwise
# SES_REGION=us-east-1                   # Amazon SES (infra/aws-ses/README.md); SES_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY stay in Infisical
# SES_FROM=                              # dark until SES creds live AND EMAIL_PROVIDER set; until then getEmailClient() uses Resend (lib/email/index.ts)
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=ses                     # forces SES once creds live; omit to auto-prefer SES when configured, or set 'resend' to force-rollback
